{"obs_mql4yqkd_4fda6efdee90":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_call","id":"obs_mql4yqkd_4fda6efdee90","raw":{"args_preview":"{\"name\":\"github-workflows\"}","duration_ms":19,"error_message":null,"is_error":false,"result_preview":"{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"github-workflows\", \"description\": \"Complete GitHub workflow: auth setup, repo management, PR lifecycle, code review, issues. Covers gh CLI and curl fallbacks.\", \"tags\": [\"GitHub\", \"PR\", \"Issues\", \"Review\", \"Auth\", \"Repos\", \"CI/CD\"], \"related_skills\": [], \"content\": \"---\\nname: github-workflows\\ndescription: \\\"Complete GitHub workflow: auth setup, repo management, PR lifecycle, code review, issues. Covers gh CLI and curl fallbacks.\\\"\\nversion: 1.0.0\\nauthor: Hermes Agent\\nlicense: MIT\\nmetadata:\\n  hermes:\\n    tags: [GitHub, PR, Issues, Review, Auth, Repos, CI/CD]\\n---\\n\\n# GitHub Workflows\\n\\nComplete reference for all GitHub operations. Use the appropriate subsection based on what you need to accomplish.\\n\\n## Sections\\n\\n### Authentication (`references/github-auth.md`)\\nSetting up `gh` CLI or `git`+`curl` auth. HTTPS tokens, SSH keys, credential helpers. The detection pattern used by all other sections. Read this first if you get \\\"Authentication failed\\\" ...","status":"ok","task_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd","tool_call_id":"call_e7657afd522d44ebb5897c7c","tool_name":"skill_view","turn_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd:20260619_110141_5312bd:768618f4"},"sessionId":"20260619_112112_c73c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-19T16:21:19.733943+00:00"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mql4z12z_22664448bc8d":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_call","id":"obs_mql4z12z_22664448bc8d","raw":{"args_preview":"{\"url\":\"https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent\"}","duration_ms":5765,"error_message":null,"is_error":false,"result_preview":"{\"success\": true, \"url\": \"https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent\", \"title\": \"GitHub - NousResearch/hermes-agent: The agent that grows with you Â· GitHub\", \"stealth_warning\": \"Running WITHOUT residential proxies. Bot detection may be more aggressive. Consider upgrading Browserbase plan for proxy support.\", \"stealth_features\": [\"local\"], \"snapshot\": \"- generic\\n  - link \\\"Skip to content\\\" [ref=e1]\\n  - banner\\n    - heading \\\"Navigation Menu\\\" [level=2, ref=e5]\\n    - generic\\n      - link \\\"Homepage\\\" [ref=e9]\\n      - navigation \\\"Global\\\" [ref=e11]\\n        - list\\n          - listitem [level=1]\\n            - generic\\n              - button \\\"Platform\\\" [expanded=false, ref=e346]\\n          - listitem [level=1]\\n            - generic\\n              - button \\\"Solutions\\\" [expanded=false, ref=e347]\\n          - listitem [level=1]\\n            - generic\\n              - button \\\"Resources\\\" [expanded=false, ref=e348]\\n          - listitem [level=1]\\n            - generic\\n       ...","status":"ok","task_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd","tool_call_id":"call_03902298f8234390bc6d91a4","tool_name":"browser_navigate","turn_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd:20260619_110141_5312bd:768618f4"},"sessionId":"20260619_112112_c73c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-19T16:21:33.353940+00:00"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mql4z6oe_e323a1a0fc77":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_call","id":"obs_mql4z6oe_e323a1a0fc77","raw":{"args_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/.hermes/hermes-agent && git remote -v\"}","duration_ms":361,"error_message":null,"is_error":false,"result_preview":"{\"output\": \"origin\\thttps://github.com/tgunr/hermes-agent.git (fetch)\\norigin\\thttps://github.com/tgunr/hermes-agent.git (push)\\nupstream\\thttps://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.git (fetch)\\nupstream\\thttps://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.git (push)\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"error\": null}","status":"ok","task_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd","tool_call_id":"call_f50486f94f6e47419bdb32bf","tool_name":"terminal","turn_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd:20260619_110141_5312bd:768618f4"},"sessionId":"20260619_112112_c73c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-19T16:21:40.610906+00:00"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mql50p82_1cd49645a0de":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_call","id":"obs_mql50p82_1cd49645a0de","raw":{"args_preview":"{\"path\":\"~/.hermes/hermes-agent/hermes_cli/web_server.py\",\"offset\":11170,\"limit\":60}","duration_ms":121,"error_message":null,"is_error":false,"result_preview":"{\"content\": \"11170|\\n11171|    `profile` (when set) scopes the ENTIRE chat to that profile by pointing\\n11172|    ``HERMES_HOME`` at the profile dir in the child env. Every spawned\\n11173|    process (the TUI and the ``tui_gateway.entry`` it launches) resolves\\n11174|    ``get_hermes_home()`` from that env var at its own import, so the child\\n11175|    binds the profile's config, skills, memory, and state.db from the start\\n11176|    â€” the same propagation ``hermes -p <name>`` performs. The in-process\\n11177|    ``HERMES_TUI_GATEWAY_URL`` attach is SKIPPED for scoped chats: the\\n11178|    dashboard's in-memory gateway runs under the dashboard's own profile,\\n11179|    so a profile-scoped chat must spawn its own gateway subprocess.\\n11180|    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n11181|    from hermes_cli.main import PROJECT_ROOT, _make_tui_argv\\n11182|\\n11183|    profile_dir: Optional[Path] = None\\n11184|    requested = (profile or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n11185|    if requested and requested.lower() != \\\"current\\\":\\n11186| ...","status":"ok","task_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd","tool_call_id":"call_187830da09b2401b83b7d63c","tool_name":"read_file","turn_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd:20260619_110141_5312bd:768618f4"},"sessionId":"20260619_112112_c73c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-19T16:22:51.308936+00:00"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mql51efk_bed8748f30c0":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_call","id":"obs_mql51efk_bed8748f30c0","raw":{"args_preview":"{\"mode\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"~/.hermes/hermes-agent/hermes_cli/web_server.py\",\"old_string\":\"    argv, cwd = _make_tui_argv(PROJECT_ROOT / \\\"ui-tui\\\", tui_dev=False)\\n    env = os.environ.copy()\\n    try:\\n        from hermes_cli.config import apply_terminal_config_to_env\\n        apply_terminal_config_to_env(env=env)\\n    except Exception:\\n        _log.debug(\\\"Failed to apply terminal config bridge for dashboard chat\\\", exc_info=True)\\n    env.setdefault(\\\"NODE_ENV\\\", \\\"production\\\")\\n    # Browse...","duration_ms":4528,"error_message":null,"is_error":false,"result_preview":"{\"success\": true, \"diff\": \"--- a//Users/davec/.hermes/hermes-agent/hermes_cli/web_server.py\\n+++ b//Users/davec/.hermes/hermes-agent/hermes_cli/web_server.py\\n@@ -11187,11 +11187,30 @@\\n \\n     argv, cwd = _make_tui_argv(PROJECT_ROOT / \\\"ui-tui\\\", tui_dev=False)\\n     env = os.environ.copy()\\n+    \\n+    # Set HERMES_HOME in env BEFORE applying terminal config bridge.\\n+    # This ensures the subprocess gets the correct terminal.cwd from the\\n+    # target profile's config, not the dashboard's current profile.\\n+    if profile_dir is not None:\\n+        env[\\\"HERMES_HOME\\\"] = str(profile_dir)\\n+        # Temporarily set os.environ HERMES_HOME so apply_terminal_config_to_env\\n+        # reads the profile's config.yaml (read_raw_config uses os.environ)\\n+        original_hermes_home = os.environ.get(\\\"HERMES_HOME\\\")\\n+        os.environ[\\\"HERMES_HOME\\\"] = str(profile_dir)\\n+    \\n     try:\\n         from hermes_cli.config import apply_terminal_config_to_env\\n         apply_terminal_confi...","status":"ok","task_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd","tool_call_id":"call_80af328e8b5f4c53a4d03b4d","tool_name":"patch","turn_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd:20260619_110141_5312bd:768618f4"},"sessionId":"20260619_112112_c73c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-19T16:23:23.975036+00:00"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mql53bms_02d1285da01a":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_call","id":"obs_mql53bms_02d1285da01a","raw":{"args_preview":"{\"action\":\"patch\",\"name\":\"hermes-workspace-context\",\"new_string\":\"**Fix:** Shell init script at `~/.hermes/scripts/profile_cwd_sync.sh` \\u2014 sourced via `terminal.shell_init_files` on every profile. On shell start, it:\\n1. Reads `HERMES_HOME/config.yaml` for `terminal.cwd`\\n2. If set and directory exists, `cd`s there and exports `TERMINAL_CWD`\\n3. If `terminal.cwd` is not set, does nothing (keeps current behavior)\\n\\n**Upstream PR:** https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/49153 \\u20...","duration_ms":7,"error_message":null,"is_error":false,"result_preview":"{\"success\": true, \"message\": \"Patched SKILL.md in skill 'hermes-workspace-context' (1 replacement).\", \"_change\": {\"old\": \"**Fix:** Shell init script at `~/.hermes/scripts/profile_cwd_sync.sh` â€” sourced via `terminal.shell_init_files` on every profile. On shell start, it:\\n1. Reads `HERMES_HOME/config.yaml` for `terminal.câ€¦\", \"new\": \"**Fix:** Shell init script at `~/.hermes/scripts/profile_cwd_sync.sh` â€” sourced via `terminal.shell_init_files` on every profile. On shell start, it:\\n1. Reads `HERMES_HOME/config.yaml` for `terminal.câ€¦\"}}","status":"ok","task_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd","tool_call_id":"call_70a2e9a5bc104fe5a3e7d348","tool_name":"skill_manage","turn_id":"20260619_110141_5312bd:20260619_110141_5312bd:768618f4"},"sessionId":"20260619_112112_c73c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-19T16:24:53.663023+00:00"},"type":"raw"}}␀␀␀‰’␀␀tÛÿÿ